/*
 * Legacy specialty jutsu — the signature technique each of the 100 Legacies
 * grants. Equipped in the dedicated legacy slot (outside the 15-jutsu loadout),
 * usable in PvP, PvE, and Battle Towers.
 *
 * Tier rules (locked by design):
 *   • every legacy jutsu has cooldown 10 (vs 7 for starters — signatures cycle
 *     slower and hit harder);
 *   • Mythic    = S-rank percents: capped tags at 40   (bloodlineRank "S Rank")
 *   • Legendary = one tag 40 + one tag 35              (bloodlineRank "S Rank")
 *   • Rare      = all capped tags at 35                (bloodlineRank "A Rank")
 *   • Basic     = all capped tags at 30                (no rank / global caps)
 *   • Wound follows its own rank ladder: S 35 / A 30 / basic 25 (woundCapForJutsu).
 *   • Damage EP: basic 36 / rare 38 / legendary 40 / mythic 42 (all ≤ the 50 legit max).
 *     Move retains the engine's 40-EP cap; the mythic leap earns range 5 instead.
 *     60 AP = 250/250 costs, 40 AP utility = EP 0, 125/125 (starter conventions).
 *
 * Element is "None" on all 100: a Legacy can be earned by ANY build, so its
 * signature must never be element-locked out (canEquipElementJutsu always passes
 * element "None") and never swing with weather.
 *
 * Typing:
 *   • Style Legacies (taijutsu / bukijutsu / genjutsu / ninjutsu categories) are
 *     TYPED to their discipline and carry "Increase Discipline" — the style-locked
 *     offense amp. Their eligibility already requires that discipline's kills/damage,
 *     so a fixed type can never mismatch the earner's build.
 *   • Non-style DAMAGE signatures are stored as type "Any" — the ADAPTIVE marker.
 *     The legacy-slot resolver stamps the owner's trained specialty at battle time
 *     on BOTH engines (stampLegacyJutsuType below; the server mirrors it), because
 *     server getOffense has no "Any" branch and would silently scale as Ninjutsu.
 *   • 40 AP utilities stay "Any" per the utility convention (zero-damage).
 *
 * Shapes: SINGLE strike, AOE_BURST nova (full damage splashes to adjacent enemies
 * in Battle Towers — the PvE-leaning signature), Move + AOE_CIRCLE (dash to a hex,
 * ring damage on landing), and 40 AP two-tag utilities. Bloodline-unique control
 * tags (Stun, Seals, Mirror, Copy, Lag, Overclock, Pierce, the Prevents' offensive
 * halves) are deliberately absent — legacy signatures reach bloodline STRENGTH,
 * not bloodline CONTROL (PvP-balance line).
 *
 * Jutsu ids are `legacy-<slug>`; art at /legacy/jutsu/<slug>.webp (docs/legacy-assets.md §3).
 * The legacyId ↔ jutsu link also lives server-side on each def's specialtyJutsuId
 * (api/_legacy-defs.ts) — the lint test holds both sides together.
 */

